WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.301
-Our first guest is
an Oscar-nominated,

00:00:02.301 --> 00:00:04.303
Golden Globe,
and Emmy-winning actress

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:08.407
whose blockbuster films include
"Basic Instinct," "Casino."

00:00:08.407 --> 00:00:11.343
She stars in the new
television series, "Ratched,"

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:13.646
which premieres this Friday
on Netflix.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.817
It is a pleasure to welcome
the one and only Sharon Stone.

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.752
-Hey!
-Hi!

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.754
Oh, you're the best.
-Hi, son.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:24.257
-Ha! I love it!
I'm totally gonna bring that up.

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:27.226
Oh, my God, I love you.
How are you doing?

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.628
How is --
-I am okay.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.296
How are you?
Where are you?

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.366
-We're in the studio.
And I appreciate you coming on,

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:36.236
because I know you're
in quarantine in L.A.,

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:39.105
and it's a very scary time
with everything going on.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.108
-We have to be happy
in the face of disaster.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.010
It's all we have.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.146
-Our state is burning down.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:49.882
Two states over is burning down.
We have no assistance.

00:00:49.882 --> 00:00:53.586
It's -- I've never --
I just don't even know.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.020
So, yesterday --

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.690
I was just in tears yesterday
'cause we had a fire.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.793
We're in a cul-de-sac street,
and we had a fire

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:05.031
in our abutting street,
a house burning down.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:10.036
And I had to -- you know,
I had thermoses, water bottles.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.872
"Kids, you have to pack
a go bag."

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.308
And, you know,
we didn't have to leave,

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.009
but I walked through the house

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:19.212
and did that after
I got the kids in bed,

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.248
look at saying goodbye to,
you know,

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:25.651
everything we've put
our lives into making

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.854
for our families and just say
goodbye to everything

00:01:28.854 --> 00:01:31.491
in a calm way by myself.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.593
Like, we're just gonna
get in the car

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.027
with the clothes on our back.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:38.631
Everybody knew they could take
one bag and that's it,

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:39.933
because we live
in this cul-de-sac,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.368
and if we have to go,
we just have to go.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.604
And we had to make
these decisions,

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.973
and I had to have this talk
with my boys, like,

00:01:47.973 --> 00:01:52.678
"Put your computer
and one pair of shoes,

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:55.681
couple pairs of jeans
and T-shirts and a sweater,

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.317
and we're gonna go.

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.951
And there isn't
any sentimentality.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.787
We're leaving everything.
Let's go.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.888
And we have to be ready,
because there's not gonna --

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:05.691
Make sure the cars
all have gas, and that's it.

00:02:05.691 --> 00:02:09.562
And this isn't an exaggeration
when you have three states --

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.998
600 fires in our own state.

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:15.734
-I can't even imagine.
I have friends in L.A.,

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:19.305
and they were just saying
it's just bizarre.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:23.276
And, like, the --
You can't go outside because --

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.512
-It's raining ash
even in the house.

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:30.149
-Sharon, this is just --
-This is what we're breathing.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:36.088
-Ugh. I want to get to some
happier things to talk about.

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.824
-[ Laughing ]
-If you don't mind.

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.026
-You want to talk about
my monkey?

00:02:41.026 --> 00:02:43.629
-I do. I want to talk about
your monkey.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:46.665
Your co-star is a monkey.
I want to get to that.

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:49.768
First, I just want to say, and I
always bring this up to you.

00:02:49.768 --> 00:02:54.773
We were in a movie together,
and you were cast as my mom.

00:02:54.773 --> 00:02:56.743
As my mother.
-As your mommy.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.778
-In flashbacks.
Clearly, flashbacks.

00:02:58.778 --> 00:03:02.414
I wasn't in a scene with you,
but it was a kid and you were --

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:06.652
And my mother, when she found
out that you were cast

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:11.957
to play my mom,
she was like, "Finally!

00:03:11.957 --> 00:03:15.661
Finally, some accurate casting.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:21.300
I look exactly
like Sharon Stone."

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.936
And I was like --
She told everybody.

00:03:23.936 --> 00:03:25.237
People didn't even
have to bring it up.

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:26.605
She's like,
"You know who's playing me?"

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:30.109
And I go, "Yeah, Mom,
stop telling everyone this."

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.911
You were so nice to me
and so great.

00:03:32.911 --> 00:03:34.780
I loved being around you.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.850
And you know what I loved, too?
Is that you're real.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:42.254
You are exactly who you
read about in the magazines.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:43.822
-Some of it.
-Just as gorgeous in person.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.325
Yeah, some of it.
No, I mean the good stuff.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:50.463
I want to talk about "Ratched,"
because when I heard the --

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.599
-It's so good?
-You are getting rave reviews,

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.935
and congrats,
and you deserve it.

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:59.639
I was like, Ryan Murphy,
Nurse Ratched, what is he --

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:02.074
-Sarah Paulson.
-Sarah Paulson.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.575
I go, "What are you cooking up?
Sharon Stone?"

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:06.178
-The wonderful Sarah Paulson...
-It's like the --

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:09.115
-...Judy Davis, Cynthia Nixon,
Amanda Plummer.

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.450
Are you kidding?
-How --

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.018
-I gotta get Ryan Murphy
on the show,

00:04:13.018 --> 00:04:15.788
because I love
everything he does.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:19.192
He is so --
He has such a great vision.

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.628
Yeah, exactly.
And I heard that he wrote

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.631
this part for you,
which is kind of funny.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.599
-I'm not sure.
You know, after I went through

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:29.635
the majority of the press junket
and people kept saying,

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:31.370
"He wrote this part for you,"
and I was like, "Yeah."

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:32.638
And it was
a little nerve-racking,

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:33.839
and it was a little this,"
and then,

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:36.009
when we finished the junket,
I was like,

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.043
"I'm not sure how if I should --

00:04:38.043 --> 00:04:41.047
How should I feel about that he
wrote that part for me?"

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:44.116
-"Is this a compliment?"
-I back here going...

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.552
-[ Laughing ]
Because you really go for it.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.589
-"He wrote that part for me."
-No, I think he just knows

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:52.091
that you could get there
as an actor.

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.593
And man, oh, man.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:57.396
-I can play super nuts
better than anybody.

00:04:57.396 --> 00:05:02.668
-What I've seen is, like --
I go, "Oh, my gosh. Of course."

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:06.472
I mean, you just nail it.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.941
Here is Sharon Stone
in "Ratched," on Netflix.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:12.011
With Corey Stoll.
-Take a look.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.780
-I can't rest
until I know he's dead.

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.783
-Well, I gotta say,
for a quarter million dollars,

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:19.819
I'm confident
I can make that happen.

00:05:21.821 --> 00:05:23.856
-Hmm.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:34.299
I want you to decapitate him.

00:05:34.299 --> 00:05:38.671
Once his head is removed,
I want you to bring it to me.

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.207
Of course there'll be
logistics involved,

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:44.944
and discretion
is extremely paramount.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:49.315
But, of course, you know that.

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:56.021
♪♪

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.091
I want to give his head
to my son

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.993
as a gift for his 21st birthday.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.728
♪♪

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:06.632
-Congrats on "Ratched,"
and I'm so happy to talk to you,

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.268
hopefully next time in person.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.703
Sharon Stone, everybody.

00:06:10.703 --> 00:06:13.206
"Ratched" premieres
this Friday on Netflix.

